  "dom_id": "step-q94116",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ b & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)=-2{x}_{1}^{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}\\,$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b?$",
  "worked_solution": "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =-2{x}_{1}^{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =(-2){x}_{1}^{2}+(-5){x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,(-5){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+(-3){x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must split the coefficient of $-10{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries \n\n$$\n{a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{-10}{2}=-5\n$$\n\nof our matrix. So, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -5 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-2$ and $b=-5.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b=-2+(-5)=-7.\n$$",
